/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Size the plan with service loads: A = (P + Wf)/qs, where P is the column load, Wf the footing weight (start with 10 % of P) and qs the safe bearing capacity.
   - With a column moment M (service), the pressure varies across the length: p = (P + Wf)/A ± M/Z, with Z = BL²/6 for bending along L.
   - Use the net factored pressure wu = Pu/A (or the trapezoid from Pu and Mu); the footing weight is left out.
   - In a rectangular pad the long bars are spread evenly across B.
   - A large pad can be thick at the column and taper to an edge of at least 150 mm (IS 456 clause 34.1.2).
*/
