/* book Worked example: Q: A 300 mm × 500 mm column carries a service load of 1200 kN. The safe bearing capacity is 200 kN/m². Design a rectangular footing with M20 concrete and Fe415 bars.
   1. Plan: A = 1.1 × 1200/200 = 6.60 m². Equal projections need L − B = 0.5 − 0.3 = 0.2 m, so B(B + 0.2) = 6.60, B = 2.47 m. Adopt L × B = 2.7 m × 2.5 m = 6.75 m²; both projections are (2.7 − 0.5)/2 = (2.5 − 0.3)/2 = 1.10 m.
   2. Net factored pressure: wu = 1.5 × 1200/6.75 = 266.67 kN/m².
   3. Moment per metre at either face: 266.67 × 1.10²/2 = 161.33 kN·m/m; d for bending = √(161.33 × 10⁶/2760) = 242 mm. Punching alone would need d ≈ 440 mm; one-way shear needs more. Adopt D = 600 mm, d = 600 − 50 − 16 = 534 mm (average of the two layers).
   4. One-way shear at d from the long face: Vu = 266.67 × 2.5 × (1.10 − 0.534) = 377.3 kN, τv = 377333/(2500 × 534) = 0.283 N/mm². With 11 bars of 16 mm, pt = 0.166 % and τc = 0.293 N/mm² ≥ τv. The other direction gives the same stress.
   5. Punching: Vu = 1800 − 266.67 × (0.5 + 0.534)(0.3 + 0.534) = 1570.0 kN, b0 = 2(500 + 300 + 2 × 534) = 3736 mm, τv = 0.787 N/mm². ks = 0.5 + 300/500 = 1.1 → 1.0; allowed 0.25√20 = 1.118 N/mm². Safe.
   6. Steel along L (moment 403.3 kN·m on 2.5 m): Ast = 2165 mm² (minimum 1800); 11 bars of 16 mm = 2212 mm². Steel along B (moment 435.6 kN·m on 2.7 m): 2338 mm² (minimum 1944); 12 bars of 16 mm = 2413 mm².
   7. Central band: β = 2.7/2.5 = 1.08, 2/(β + 1) = 0.962, so 11.5 → 12 of the 12 short bars go in the central 2.5 m band; with β this close to 1 the spacing is almost uniform.
   8. Anchorage: Ld of a 16 mm bar = 47 × 16 = 752 mm < 1100 − 50 = 1050 mm available. Bearing under the column: 1800 × 10³/(300 × 500) = 12.0 N/mm² ≤ 0.45 × 20 × 2 = 18.0 N/mm².
   9. Soil with the real weight: (1200 + 6.75 × 0.6 × 25)/6.75 = 192.8 kN/m² ≤ 200.
   Answer: Footing 2.7 m × 2.5 m × 600 mm; 11 bars of 16 mm along the 2.7 m length and 12 bars of 16 mm along the 2.5 m width; one-way shear 0.28 ≤ 0.29 N/mm² and punching 0.79 ≤ 1.12 N/mm². */
