/* book Worked example 2: Q: A 400 mm square column carries a service load of 900 kN and a service moment of 90 kN·m. The safe bearing capacity is 200 kN/m². Size a rectangular footing with the moment along its length, and find the factored design moment at the column face in that direction.
   1. e = M/P = 90/900 = 0.10 m. Try L × B = 2.8 m × 2.2 m: A = 6.16 m², Z = 2.2 × 2.8²/6 = 2.875 m³, L/6 = 0.467 m > e.
   2. Service pressures (10 % self-weight): (900 + 90)/6.16 ± 90/2.875 = 160.7 ± 31.3: pmax = 192.0 ≤ 200 and pmin = 129.4 kN/m² > 0. (A 2.6 m length gives 209 kN/m², too high.)
   3. Net factored pressures: 1350/6.16 ± 135/2.875: q1 = 266.1 and q2 = 172.2 kN/m².
   4. At the column face on the heavy side, 1.20 m from the edge: qf = 266.1 − (266.1 − 172.2) × 1.20/2.8 = 225.9 kN/m².
   5. Moment of the trapezoid: Mu = B[qfx²/2 + (q1 − qf)x²/3] = 2.2 × [225.9 × 1.20²/2 + 40.3 × 1.20²/3] = 400.3 kN·m. Using the average pressure instead would give only 347.1 kN·m.
   Answer: 2.8 m × 2.2 m; service pressures 192 and 129 kN/m²; design moment at the heavy face 400 kN·m on the 2.2 m width. */
