/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - With the centroid under the resultant, the factored soil pressure is uniform: qu = (Pu1 + Pu2)/(LB), and the line load along the footing is w = quB.
   - Draw the shear force and bending moment diagrams of a beam of length L carrying the upward line load w and the two downward column loads.
   - a term in brackets counts only once x has passed that column; M positive means tension at the bottom.
   - Across the width the column load spreads out to the edges, so a strip under each column works as a cantilever of length (B − b)/2 from the column face, loaded by Pu/B per metre of width.
*/
