/* book Worked example: Q: Two 400 mm square columns, 3.0 m apart, carry service loads of 600 kN and 900 kN. The safe bearing capacity is 150 kN/m² (net) and the footing width is fixed at 2.0 m. Design the rectangular combined footing in M20 concrete with Fe415 bars.
   1. Area A = 1500/150 = 10.0 m²; with B = 2.0 m, L = 5.0 m.
   2. Resultant from the 600 kN column: x̄ = 900 × 3/1500 = 1.80 m. Projections: a1 = 2.5 − 1.80 = 0.70 m and a2 = 5.0 − 3.0 − 0.70 = 1.30 m.
   3. Factored loads 900 and 1350 kN; qu = 2250/(5 × 2) = 225 kN/m²; w = 225 × 2.0 = 450 kN/m.
   4. Shear: V = 315 kN just left of column 1 and -585 kN just right; V = 0 at x = 900/450 = 2.00 m; 765 kN just left of column 2 and -585 kN just right; zero at the far end.
   5. Moments: 110.25 kN·m (sagging) under column 1; 270 kN·m hogging at x = 2.0 m; 380.25 kN·m sagging under column 2 (centre values, slightly on the safe side).
   6. Depth: one-way shear governs. Adopt D = 700 mm, d = 700 − 50 − 8 = 642 mm. The largest shear at d from a face is left of column 2: Vu = 386.1 kN, τv = 386100/(2000 × 642) = 0.301 N/mm².
   7. Bottom steel for 380 kN·m: Ast = 1686 mm², just above the minimum 0.0012 × 2000 × 700 = 1680 mm²; provide 9 bars of 16 mm = 1810 mm².
   8. Top steel for 270 kN·m: Ast = 1188 mm², below the minimum, so 9 bars would do for bending. But the governing shear section (2.86 m from the end) has a hogging moment of 104 kN·m, so the top bars are its tension steel: 9 bars give pt = 0.141 % and τc = 0.280 < 0.301 N/mm². Provide 12 bars of 16 mm = 2413 mm², pt = 0.188 %, τc = 0.310 N/mm² ≥ τv.
   9. Punching at the 1350 kN column: Vu = 1350 − 225 × (1.042)² = 1105.7 kN, b0 = 4 × 1042 = 4168 mm, τv = 0.413 ≤ 1.118 N/mm².
   10. Transverse under column 2: cantilever (2.0 − 0.4)/2 = 0.8 m, load 1350/2.0 = 675 kN/m, Mu = 675 × 0.8²/2 = 216 kN·m on a strip 0.4 + 2 × 0.642 = 1.68 m wide, d = 626 mm: Ast = 974 mm², minimum 1415 mm²: 8 bars of 16 mm. Under column 1: 144 kN·m, 8 bars of 16 mm.
   Answer: Footing 5.0 m × 2.0 m × 700 mm, projections 0.70 m and 1.30 m; 9 bars of 16 mm at the bottom and 12 at the top lengthwise (the top bars raised for shear); 8 and 8 transverse 16 mm bars under the heavy and light columns; all shear checks pass. */
